# Local development only. Never commit the real .dev.vars.
#
# Copy this to .dev.vars and fill it in:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# For the deployed Worker these are set with `npx wrangler secret put NAME`
# instead, one at a time. They are never in a file that git can see.

# REQUIRED. Shared with whatever drives your printer: the browser bridge, the
# Raspberry Pi agent, or the Pico. Anything holding this can take messages out
# of your queue, so generate a real one:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
PRINTER_TOKEN=change-me-openssl-rand-base64-32

# REQUIRED. Gets you into /admin, where you approve messages.
ADMIN_TOKEN=change-me-too

# REQUIRED. Salts the hash used for rate limiting, so the database never holds
# anybody's address. Changing it resets everyone's daily allowance.
IP_SALT=change-me-as-well

# Optional. Signs the proof-of-work challenges. Falls back to IP_SALT.
# ALTCHA_HMAC_KEY=

# Optional. The private door: a link ending in #k=<this> opens the form while
# the service is closed to everybody else. See docs/07-operating.md.
# ACCESS_KEY=

# Optional. Where messages waiting for your approval are announced. Leave both
# unset and the admin page is the only place you will see them.
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK=  (paste the whole webhook URL Discord gives you)
# NTFY_TOPIC=some-topic-nobody-will-guess
